# Phase 325 (STOR-01) — sudoers grant for the gocryptfs (encrypted folders) wrapper.
# Security model: grant on ONE explicit binary path, NO glob, NO arg wildcard.
# The wrapper validates its action enum {install|create|unlock|lock|status},
# regex-validates + data-root-anchors every path arg, and builds every
# gocryptfs/fusermount/apt argv itself. The passphrase reaches gocryptfs via stdin
# (-extpass reading a private env var), NEVER argv — so no caller string can escape
# into a privileged command. A trailing `*` here would be a hole (see
# sudoers.d/livos-smart header) — there is deliberately none.
# Deploy: deploy-livinityd.sh block 2a/2b-crypto; day-2: update.sh Step 7.10f.
Cmnd_Alias LIVINITYD_CRYPTO = /usr/local/lib/livos/livos-crypto.sh
bruce ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: LIVINITYD_CRYPTO
